    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d41">

                <pb facs="0150" n="62" sameAs="frus:frus1892/pg62"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Egan to Mr. Foster.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Santiago</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1892-07-11"><hi rendition="#italic">July 11,
                        1892</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Mr. Egan reports that an indemnity for the seamen of the <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Baltimore</hi> has been agreed to by the minister for foreign affairs, who
                    this day offers $75,000 in gold, and that the Congress will be asked, without
                    delay, for the approval to which the offer is subject. Mr. Egan recommends that
                    it be accepted and confirmed at once.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
